API-18: openswmm-legacy (runswmm) exits with status 1 when the run fails

main() of the legacy command line program is documented to return the error
status, but it always returned 0; it only printed "There are errors." when
swmm_getError() reported an error. Keep the code swmm_getError() returns and
exit with 1 when it is non-zero, so scripts can detect a failed run without
parsing the report.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply API-18_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/cli/main.c b/src/legacy/cli/main.c
index 01ff2c5..3b32213 100644
--- a/src/legacy/cli/main.c
+++ b/src/legacy/cli/main.c
@@ -37,6 +37,7 @@ int  main(int argc, char *argv[])
     char blank[] = "";
     char errMsg[128];
     int  msgLen = 127;
+    int  errorCode = 0;
     time_t start;
     double runTime;
 
@@ -90,7 +91,8 @@ int  main(int argc, char *argv[])
         // Display closing status on console
         runTime = difftime(time(0), start);
         printf("\n\n... OPEN-SOURCE SWMM completed in %.2f seconds.", runTime);
-        if      ( swmm_getError(errMsg, msgLen) > 0 ) printf(" There are errors.\n");
+        errorCode = swmm_getError(errMsg, msgLen);
+        if      ( errorCode > 0 ) printf(" There are errors.\n");
         else if ( swmm_getWarnings() > 0 ) printf(" There are warnings.\n");
         else printf("\n");
     }
@@ -101,5 +103,6 @@ int  main(int argc, char *argv[])
     getchar();
 */
 
-    return 0;
+    // --- exit status tells the caller whether the run failed
+    return errorCode ? 1 : 0;
 }
\ No newline at end of file
